# Build output
node_modules/
dist/
release/
release-signing-test/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Signing material. A .pfx must never reach the repository, and a signed build
# produced with a throwaway certificate must never be mistaken for a release.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.cer
*.pvk
*.key
*.spc
*.p7b
*.p7c
# A base64 copy of a key is the same key. *.pfx does not match "name.pfx.base64",
# so a file exported for transport or for a CI secret would otherwise be staged
# by accident, and it is the private half that must never be committed.
*.pfx.base64
*.p12.base64
*.pem.base64
*.key.base64

# The update signing key. The public half is committed on purpose, at
# assets/update-public-key.pem, because the application has to verify with it.
# The private half must never be in the repository: it is the only thing that
# can sign a release, and anyone holding it could offer a malicious update to
# every installation. The real one is written to ~/.novaris by
# scripts/create-update-key.mjs.
update-signing-key.pem
*-private-key.pem
*update-signing*.pem

# Local environments and secrets. Nothing in this project needs a committed
# key, and the vault and profile are per-machine, so these must never be added.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.keystore
novaris-data.json
novaris-vault.bin

# The one key that must be tracked. Git applies the last matching rule, so this
# has to come after the *.pem above rather than before it: placed earlier it was
# silently overridden, the public key was never committed, and a fresh clone would
# have produced a build with no key that refuses every update.
!assets/update-public-key.pem
novaris-data.json.*
novaris-vault.bin.*

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs and diagnostics
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
crashpad/
*.dmp

# Test and coverage output
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Local scratch
tmp/
.cache/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
